# What not to upload to the build. Without this file the host generates its own
# default, which is a fine default but knows nothing about this project - and in
# particular knows nothing about data/.

# Reinstalled by npm during the build, so uploading it is pure waste. 40M here,
# and 19M of that is playwright, which is not even a dependency of this app.
node_modules

# History the running container has no use for.
.git

# Continuous integration config. Runs on GitHub, not in the container.
.github

# The database. This is the entry with a reason beyond size: /app/data is where
# the disk gets mounted, so anything shipped there sits under a mount point and
# makes "is the disk working?" unanswerable. And an image is an artifact that
# gets copied around - real accounts do not belong in one.
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Secrets. There is no .env in this checkout today; this is here so there never
# is one in an image either.
.env
.env.local

# Build and run noise.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and operating-system residue. Guards - none of these are checked in.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
